/**
 * Corporate & Business Events — one blueprint per occasion.
 *
 * Thirty-five occasions, the largest category in the catalogue, and the
 * one where the same five words in the catalogue cover genuinely
 * different events. Eleven of these share the "conference" template and
 * almost nothing else: an AGM is a statutory meeting with a quorum and a
 * scrutineer, a sales kick-off is a motivation event with a party at the
 * end, and a dealer meet is both of those plus travel for two hundred
 * people. They are written here as the different things they are.
 *
 * What shapes this category:
 *
 *   · Confidentiality is a first-class answer. A board meeting, an
 *     investor meet and a strategy offsite default to no photography,
 *     no press and no stream, and we never add one back quietly.
 *   · Nothing religious is ever assumed. An office inauguration may
 *     have a ceremony or may not; we ask, and the practitioner is only
 *     ever found because the company asked for one.
 *   · Alcohol is never assumed. Where an evening might have a bar, it
 *     is a question, and the venue holds the licence.
 *   · Who is in the room decides the plan more than the budget does.
 *     Employees, clients, channel partners and press need different
 *     rooms, different hospitality and different rules about cameras.
 *   · Travel and stay for people coming in from other cities is
 *     planning we do around arrangements the company makes — we have
 *     no hotel trade and never pretend to.
 *
 * Builders and the repeating questions live in data/blueprintKit.js.
 */
